  "body": "Closes #401\nClaim: cloud/i401\n\n**Problem.** `anonymize.py --private` replaced `div#para…` bodies and MP subjects but left two copies of MP text on composer/edit-form pages: the review cell after `td.messCase1bis` and the `content_form` textarea. `check --private` did not flag either, so `publish.py` would accept a real thread's composer.\n\n**Cause.** Both positions were only handled for the MPStorage thread (`mpstorage_form_copies`).\n\n**Change.** In private mode, on a form page that is neither MPStorage nor a fixture thread, both positions are replaced by the private placeholder. A page is a fixture thread only if every `sujet` input and visible \"Sujet :\" header names `fixture-test-N`; a page naming no thread fails closed. `check --private` flags both positions in both verifiers (`findings` and an independent `_v_fixture_thread` / `_v_text`). README updated. Fixture-thread pages are left byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\n**Tests** (`PrivateFormCopyTests`, tooling/fixtures/tests): real-thread composer flagged then replaced (both copies, clean on re-check); fixture thread unchanged and unflagged; mixed names not a fixture; no thread name fails closed; attribute order and empty textarea; non-private mode keeps copies. Full suite: 197 OK.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CH8RQGy28PG2CW3u1v)_",
